<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="56776" href="schedule/2011/fall/UKR/199/56776.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2011" href="schedule/2011.xml">2011</calendarYear><term id="120118" href="schedule/2011/fall.xml">Fall 2011</term><subject id="UKR" href="schedule/2011/fall/UKR.xml">Ukrainian</subject><course id="199" href="schedule/2011/fall/UKR/199.xml">Undergraduate Open Seminar</course></parents><sectionNumber>U3 </sectionNumber><sectionDateRange>Meets 17-Oct-11 - 07-Dec-11.</sectionDateRange><creditHours>2 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Topic: Ukranian Literature in Translation. The course introduces students to major authors in Ukrainian literature of the 19th and 20th centuries. Works of Taras Shevchenko, Ivan Franko, Lesia Ukrainka, Vasyl Stefanyk, Mykhailo Kotsiubynskyi, Borys Antonenko-Davydovych, Vasyl Stus, Valeriy Shevchuk,Volodymyr Dibrova and others will be discussed. The developments in Ukrainian literature will be analyzed within the historical and socio-cultural context.</sectionText><partOfTerm>B</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2011-10-17Z</startDate><endDate>2011-12-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>03:00 PM</start><end>04:20 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>1126</roomNumber><buildingName>Foreign Languages Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Chumachenko" firstName="V">Chumachenko, V</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>